WEBVTT

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:04.400
Prepare yourself...

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.730
and say your prayers!

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:23.950
Well, if it isn't Yasaburo.

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:26.160
What are you doing in a place like this?

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.460
I just happened to be passing by.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:31.290
Pardon me, but is that you, Yasaburo-kun?

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:34.300
Shimogamo Yasaburo, at your service.

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:37.050
What brings you here?

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:41.520
You could say that my
fool's blood brought me here.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.160
Tanuki are truly foolish creatures.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.340
I will admit that they are pleasant,

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:53.030
but there is no denying
that they are fools as well.

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:56.800
That is a rather tengu-like
thing to say, Nidaime.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.830
I am not a tengu.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.980
What is a tengu?

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:03.500
That frail, old thing right there?

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:06.610
He can't control tengu
whirlwinds as he pleases,

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:08.880
and he can't even fly properly.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:12.220
His last days are spent
meaninglessly and risibly.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.490
But this is a positively pathetic sight.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:19.670
You choose to live, reliant on the
pity of creatures such as tanuki.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:21.940
You should be ashamed.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:23.450
For shame!

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:27.460
Stay right there. Don't run away.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:30.480
I'll drop you from here again!

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:33.480
You're still alive, Father?

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:37.670
If you want me dead, just try to kill me.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.150
You're not even worth killing.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.760
You can go die on your own somewhere.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:01:59.330
Good grief.

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:00.940
He ran away again.

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:02.800
How pathetic.

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:04.210
Well?

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:05.850
It's my victory, isn't it?

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.880
U-Um...

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:10.540
How did you come to that conclusion?

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:13.860
If you can't understand,
then there's no point talking to you.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:19.360
I wonder where Benten is
and how she's doing.

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:29.260
I'm sure it'll be quite fun
when she gets back.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:34.270
Now's the time when that beautiful
girl should be here more than ever.

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:37.470
I want to see Benten.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:41.160
I long to see Benten.

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:15.020
<b>Episode Two
The Conjurer Tenmaya</b>

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:17.980
<b>Mamiana Antique Shop</b>

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:20.360
Nii-chan.

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:23.010
Oh, you're done early today.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:26.270
Kaisei-neechan said that
I could go home for the day.

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:28.560
When are you going to be done, Nii-chan?

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:30.370
That all depends on Chujiro-san.

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:33.120
He left a while ago
and hasn't been back since.

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:37.380
Nii-chan, can tanuki become
English gentlemen, too?

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:38.510
What?

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:40.000
Of course not.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:45.480
Kinkaku and Ginkaku said they'd take after
the Nidaime and become English gentlemen.

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:46.850
Do you think they can?

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:48.560
Don't listen to them, Yashiro.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:50.010
You'll catch their idiocy.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:51.890
Don't make fun of my brothers!

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:53.660
Whoa!

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:57.580
Is that Kaisei?

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:59.740
Don't touch me, you moron!

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:04.250
Kaisei-neechan, aren't you hot in there?

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:08.120
I have a cold pack here with me,
so it's nice and cool in here.

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:11.160
No wonder my back felt cool.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:15.180
So I hear that Kinkaku and Ginkaku
are following the Nidaime around.

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:16.310
Hell if I know!

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:19.040
I'm sure that the Nidaime
is just lazing around, too.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:21.590
The battle at the Minami-za 
was a huge letdown.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:24.690
And I thought some great tengu
battle was going to break out.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:26.350
You never know.

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:28.890
Benten-sama will probably be back eventually.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:30.310
You're so pathetic.

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:33.390
Stop smirking just because that
half-tengu is coming back.

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:37.040
Why don't you shut your mouth,
you little squirt?

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.150
Stop! Stop!

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:38.150
Take that and that.

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:39.260
I'm going to throw up!

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:43.180
Take that and that and that.
That and that and that.

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:43.650
When are you two
going to get married, Nii-chan?

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.540
Where did that come from?

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:48.250
Of course we're not getting married.

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:50.300
Why aren't you getting married?

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:51.530
You get along so well.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:54.850
Whether we get along or not,

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:58.050
our engagement was canceled.

00:05:58.050 --> 00:05:59.120
Yeah.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:01.540
That promise doesn't matter anymore.

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:04.170
But the person who wanted to do away with it

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:06.040
was Uncle Soun, right?

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:08.800
And Uncle went off somewhere, right?

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:12.180
And Mother loves Kaisei-neechan, right?

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:14.060
Who's going to say no?

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:16.940
If you want to get married,
you should just do it.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:23.320
Yasaburo, I have a sudden job.
Would you mind?

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:27.900
Come on, now.

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:30.910
It just had to be Yasaburo?

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:36.160
<b>Tenmaya</b>

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:37.660
<b>Ramen</b>

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:42.540
<b>Tenmaya Ramen</b>

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:42.540
I want to get rid of that,
but it's out of my hands.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:44.410
What is that?

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:48.630
Lately there've been whispers of
strange phenomena going on.

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:52.550
At first, I just thought it was just
the work of some tanuki or tengu,

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:56.670
but then that thing
just popped up on the roof.

00:06:56.670 --> 00:07:00.560
So I went in to have them
take it down, but...

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:08.080
You can't just go build this
here without permission.

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:10.850
This obviously violates building laws.

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:21.590
Hey, are you listening?

00:07:22.030 --> 00:07:22.710
Huh?

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:33.300
His chin! His chin! His chin!

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:36.600
That's what happened.

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:38.360
That's truly ridiculous.

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:39.630
Sounds amusing.

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:41.600
This is no time to be amused about it.

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:44.900
All right. I'll go have a look.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.090
Be careful, Nii-chan.

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:49.570
Heya.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:50.810
Heya.

00:07:55.390 --> 00:07:56.730
Hey there, youngin'.

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:57.990
You look merry.

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:00.000
You look quite merry as well.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:01.300
Yup.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:03.370
I'm always merry.

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:08.250
That's because everything in the world
is entertainment to me.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:09.440
Oh, yeah?

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:13.220
I'm pretty confident I can top that.

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:14.320
Oho?

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:16.800
And where does that confidence come from?

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:21.100
My confidence has no source, mister.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:24.000
You seem to understand how things work.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:26.480
I don't know who you are,

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:29.630
but you're not supposed
to build something like this here.

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:34.440
The most unpleasant thing in this world

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:37.340
is getting bossed around by someone.

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:41.290
If you insist on doing this,
I'll gladly take you on.

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:44.400
Then let's play a while, mister.

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:46.170
Oh?

00:08:46.550 --> 00:08:49.170
If you close your eyes and count to three,

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:52.330
I'll show you something interesting.

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:54.520
Well, I'm looking forward to that.

00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:57.180
One...

00:08:57.590 --> 00:08:58.800
Two...

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:00.430
Three...

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:02.060
You ready?

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:10.440
You fool.

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:14.240
As if a brown bear would show up
somewhere like this.

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:15.700
To return the favor,

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:19.080
I'll show you something interesting, too.

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:23.450
Hup. Hup. Hup. Hup.

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:27.830
Hup, hup, hup, hup.

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:29.820
Hup, hup...

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:39.720
Everything in the world is entertainment!

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:45.180
Hup, hup, hup, hup...

00:09:45.590 --> 00:09:48.440
Are you actually a tengu, mister?

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:50.740
What are you talking about?

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:53.440
I'm much greater than any tengu.

00:09:58.170 --> 00:09:59.820
Wait, wait, wait!

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:03.930
H-Hey, Yasaburo?!

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:06.140
Nii-chan, what's wrong?

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:15.520
S-Stop!

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:18.860
If you don't stop, I-I'll shoot!

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:39.780
Huh?

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:42.120
What's going on?

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:47.900
Nii-chan! Nii-chan!

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:48.870
Wake up!

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:53.000
Where am I?

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.630
Nii-chan's awake!

00:10:56.120 --> 00:10:57.880
Are you okay, Nii-chan?

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:00.260
You finally woke up?

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:01.300
What?

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:02.890
What's going on?

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:04.830
You don't remember anything?

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:06.520
You were tricked!

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:08.570
We didn't know what to do.

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:11.470
You weren't responding to us at all.

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:15.220
It was Kaisei's idea
to throw you into the Kamo River.

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:17.040
Thanks, Kaisei—

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:20.230
A tanuki getting tricked
by a human is just pathetic!

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:25.030
<b>Teramachi Street</b>

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:31.560
<b>Open</b>

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:33.250
Pardon me.

00:11:42.210 --> 00:11:44.050
Hello, Professor Yodogawa.

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:45.750
Good evening.

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:48.260
Thanks for coming.

00:11:48.990 --> 00:11:51.330
I wanted to show you this painting.

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:53.560
Don't you think it's magnificent?

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:57.320
It looks like some furry rock.

00:11:58.620 --> 00:12:01.570
I must say, this is a rather unique shop.

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:05.740
It's a shop that doubles as
Master Artist Ayameike's gallery.

00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:09.700
The one who runs the
shop is his wife, though.

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:14.490
So it's a perfect meeting spot
for the Thursday Club

00:12:14.490 --> 00:12:16.590
that advocates against tanuki hot pots.

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:18.160
So...

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:21.060
Benten-san isn't back yet?

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:24.580
Well, Benten-sama is rather whimsical.

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:27.680
Let's split up and find him.

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:30.560
Ayameike-san!

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:32.100
Ayameike-san!

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:36.980
What tanuki clan are you from?

00:12:38.660 --> 00:12:42.040
I am Yasaburo, the third son
of Shimogamo Soichiro.

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:47.950
I am Onjoji Gonzaburo.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.900
Your older brother, Yaichiro-kun,
has helped me before.

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:52.630
I've heard of you as well.

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:54.890
The Master Artist is this way.

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:56.580
I shall lead you to him.

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:15.350
Be sure not to bother him.

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:22.110
How do you do, Ayameike-sensei?

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:23.870
I've come to escort you.

00:13:26.830 --> 00:13:29.800
This hollow was a pond.

00:13:30.710 --> 00:13:32.820
It was fifty years ago,

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:35.730
but I dug it up myself.

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:40.260
When I sit here like this,

00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:44.880
I feel like a frog at the bottom of a well,
and it's rather pleasant.

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:49.120
Apparently, dinner will be ready soon.

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:50.260
Let's head back.

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:53.770
That means my work is done for the day.

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:56.630
Yes, good work.

00:13:57.840 --> 00:13:58.650
Oh?

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:01.350
I hear some festivities going on.

00:14:01.990 --> 00:14:06.880
Ah, it appears that man has arrived.

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:08.150
What man?

00:14:08.150 --> 00:14:09.830
A guest.

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:15.040
Bringing the festivities along
is nothing to him.

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:21.970
It seems that the professor
hasn't returned yet.

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:25.800
It seems that he's about to get lost.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:28.680
I will go find him.

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:30.250
Right...

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:33.180
Pardon me.

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:36.150
This is Tenmaya.

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:36.810
Oh?

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:37.680
Ah!

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:38.880
What?

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:40.810
You're a guest tonight, too?

00:14:41.490 --> 00:14:43.320
I'm glad to see you again.

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:45.080
My name is Yasaburo.

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:47.940
It's a pleasure, Yasaburo-kun.

00:14:48.140 --> 00:14:51.700
Tonight, I'll treat you to some exotic foods.

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:56.690
If you leave them to me,

00:14:56.690 --> 00:14:59.210
I can sell your paintings
for any price you want.

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:01.880
I have no intention of doing that.

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:06.880
There's no point in having these paintings
in a shop where no one drops by.

00:15:07.140 --> 00:15:08.230
Sell your paintings,

00:15:08.230 --> 00:15:11.450
and you'll be able
to fill that pond that dried up.

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:13.770
You saved my life, Sensei.

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:16.510
That's why I want you to live a good life.

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:20.640
I am happy with my current life.

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:23.910
There isn't much that I can do

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:29.040
if you're a mountain hermit satisfied
playing with tanuki and rocks.

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:32.840
I'm nothing that grand.

00:15:32.840 --> 00:15:33.670
Exactly.

00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:35.950
Mountain hermit my toosh.

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:39.660
He's put me through hell and made me cry.

00:15:39.940 --> 00:15:43.560
Does this mean that you're 
a vulgar man, Sensei?

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:45.730
I am very much a vulgar man.

00:15:45.730 --> 00:15:48.440
Wonderful, wonderful!
That's how it should be!

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:50.380
Long live vulgarity!

00:15:50.730 --> 00:15:54.280
Well, for all you vulgar
fellows are gathered here,

00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:55.890
a vulgar performance!

00:15:57.390 --> 00:16:00.390
<b>Tenmaya</b>

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:02.400
Oh.

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:09.530
<b>Tenmaya</b>

00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:13.780
Oh, my!

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:17.530
<b>Tenmaya</b>

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:26.740
The end!

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:34.380
This is what you call an illusion.

00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:43.550
Professor, who is that Tenmaya fellow?

00:16:43.550 --> 00:16:46.220
I've seen him before at the Friday Club.

00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:49.690
He seemed to be working for Jyurojin.

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:51.970
No wonder he seems so shady.

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:54.070
He might be a spy.

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.300
But it's strange.

00:16:56.730 --> 00:16:59.900
Apparently he incurred Jyurojin's wrath

00:16:59.900 --> 00:17:02.080
and disappeared from Kyoto.

00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:05.230
It's been quite a few years now.

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:08.840
<b>Tenmaya</b>

00:17:11.240 --> 00:17:13.220
Yodogawa-sensei.

00:17:13.870 --> 00:17:15.590
So I heard...

00:17:15.820 --> 00:17:19.140
that you were kicked out of the Friday Club.

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:21.210
What of it, Tenmaya-san?

00:17:21.210 --> 00:17:23.350
I'm pretty sure that doesn't concern you.

00:17:24.030 --> 00:17:27.990
I hear that you're protesting
tanuki hot pots in protest.

00:17:27.990 --> 00:17:29.900
That's a gutsy move.

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:31.640
Whom did you hear that from?

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:33.360
I can see and hear everything,

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:35.110
even as far as the depths of Hell.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:38.870
Didn't you go off on a journey?

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:41.620
It's true. I did.

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:47.620
The expression of my innocent curiosity
incurred the great Jyurojin's wrath.

00:17:47.850 --> 00:17:52.630
Now I live like a drifter,
drifting like a white cloud on the wind.

00:17:52.990 --> 00:17:56.360
Let's get along, since we're both outcasts.

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:58.160
I'd be happy to hear you out.

00:17:58.160 --> 00:17:59.730
I'll decline.

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:01.890
I couldn't afford your consultation fee.

00:18:03.370 --> 00:18:04.640
Say, Professor...

00:18:05.400 --> 00:18:07.380
Jyurojin is rather frightening.

00:18:07.380 --> 00:18:09.770
You'd best watch your back.

00:18:10.390 --> 00:18:12.650
Anyway, I'll be taking my leave now.

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:22.160
What an appalling fellow.

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:24.660
We can't let our guard down.

00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:28.210
Please go ahead and head home, Professor.

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:30.690
I have to make a stop somewhere.

00:18:34.200 --> 00:18:35.170
Oh?

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:39.880
Are you done with
your disguise, Yasaburo-san?

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:42.240
So you did see through me.

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:43.930
It's nice to see you again.

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:48.690
Did you forget something?

00:18:49.660 --> 00:18:52.380
I want to know more about Tenmaya-san.

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:55.750
Tenmaya-san managed to trick me before,

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:58.700
so I'd like to get back at him.

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:01.820
Does Tenmaya-san trick tanuki?

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:03.470
He does.

00:19:03.470 --> 00:19:04.950
I went through hell.

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:06.860
What a troublesome person.

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:11.330
I will tell you from
whence Tenmaya-san came.

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:12.950
Follow me, please.

00:19:14.810 --> 00:19:19.090
I hide this here when Tenmaya-san comes by.

00:19:19.310 --> 00:19:22.730
Because he tries to burn it to ashes.

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:34.980
I received this painting
of Hell from someone.

00:19:35.260 --> 00:19:38.690
They asked me to paint the Buddha in it.

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:42.760
I don't want to paint anything
under commission from anyone,

00:19:42.760 --> 00:19:45.990
but when I saw this, I wanted to paint it in.

00:19:46.270 --> 00:19:49.450
I felt bad for the dead.

00:19:49.860 --> 00:19:52.630
So you would be his Buddha in Hell.

00:19:53.270 --> 00:19:58.200
Tenmaya-san used this
spider's thread to climb out.

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:02.670
He was in this painting of Hell.

00:20:09.010 --> 00:20:12.200
The person who asked me
to add the Buddha to this painting

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:14.630
is the chief priest from a certain temple.

00:20:14.630 --> 00:20:18.790
I don't know who the
rightful owner of the painting is.

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:22.490
...incurred the great Jyurojin's wrath.

00:20:35.390 --> 00:20:37.630
<i>I want the moon.</i>

00:20:37.930 --> 00:20:40.780
<i>Go on. Try to take it, Yasaburo.</i>

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:52.390
It's rare to get a visitor at this hour.

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:56.330
Don't you think the moon is magnificent?

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:58.970
A toast to the moon tonight.

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:08.240
Hey, Tenmaya!

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:16.120
I've come to take you back to Hell!

00:21:16.410 --> 00:21:19.000
Wait! Wait!

00:21:25.830 --> 00:21:29.010
Wait!

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:39.450
<i>Humans are most detestably terrifying.</i>

00:21:40.120 --> 00:21:42.070
<i>Nothing is more dangerous than a human</i>

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:45.010
<i>partly enlightened in the
world as a tricking match.</i>

00:21:45.920 --> 00:21:51.580
<i>Do not underestimate humans who
silently perfect the art of tricking others.</i>

00:21:52.010 --> 00:21:57.420
<i>The age when tanuki are tricked
by humans is upon us.</i>

00:23:30.920 --> 00:23:33.390
I've grown rather bored.

00:23:33.870 --> 00:23:36.510
I know. I'll write a letter.

00:23:37.520 --> 00:23:39.270
How boring.

00:23:37.520 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Episode Three
The Scent of Europe</b>
